Caching is a technique used to store frequently accessed data temporarily in a fast storage layer so the system can retrieve it quickly instead of recomputing or refetching it every time.

Simple Definition
Cache = Temporary fast storage 
Purpose:

improve speed
reduce latency
reduce database/API load

