Write-behind

Concept
Workflow 1️⃣ Application writes data → cache stores it immediately. 2️⃣ Cache queues the update for later persistence. 3️⃣ A background process flushes batched writes to the DB periodically or on trigger.
Advantages
Disadvantages
Best Use Cases



Refresh-ahead

Concept
Workflow 1️⃣ Application requests data → cache serves it. 2️⃣ Cache monitors TTL (time-to-live). 3️⃣ Before expiry, a background thread or scheduler fetches fresh data from the source. 4️⃣ Cache updates the entry, ensuring next access is instant.
Advantages
Disadvantages



🎯 Key Insight
Cache-aside → Lazy loading, simple, widely used.
Write-through → Strong consistency, higher latency.
Write-behind → High performance, eventual consistency.
Refresh-ahead → Predictive, reduces misses, but may over-fetch.

